{"No-arg canManage() method in GroupPermissionsV2 incorrectly accepts VIEW scope as sufficient for manage access, violating least-privilege and contradicting canManage(GroupModel) overload": 0.9752324223518372, "getGroupIdsWithViewPermission() uses groupResource.getId() (authorization resource UUID) instead of groupResource.getName() (actual group model ID), causing group-membership filters to return no results": 0.8911818265914917, "Unconditional group filtering incorrectly restricts user search results for administrators with global view permissions - the conditional check around group filtering logic was removed, causing admins with global view-users permissions to have search results incorrectly restricted if they also have view permissions on specific groups": 0.19261083006858826, "Performance regression in group listing due to removal of global permission check optimization - code loads and checks every single subgroup from database before pagination instead of short-circuiting when user has global view permission": 0.468726247549057, "Test assertion expects HTTP 204 NO_CONTENT instead of 201 CREATED for subgroup creation POST request in testManageAllGroups method": 0.6452611684799194, "Incorrect Javadoc for requireManageMembers method references canManageMembership instead of canManageMembers": 0.4940848648548126, "Incorrect Javadoc for UserPermissionEvaluator method documentation": 0.23329558968544006, "Inconsistent resource resolution logic - resolveGroup method only resolves by ID without fallback to name, unlike resolveUser and resolveClient which fall back to username/clientId": 0.4579036235809326, "Event listener for cleaning up permissions of deleted resources only checks ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ feature flag, not ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ_V2, causing orphaned permission data when V2 is enabled without V1": 0.37375664710998535, "Logic error drops global canView() short-circuit in GroupsResource - new code uses groupsEvaluator::canView method reference which only performs per-group evaluation, filtering out groups for admins with global view rights": 0.08169594407081604, "Double-close on Response occurs when callers wrap response in try-with-resources and pass to handleCreatedResponse which also auto-closes via its own try-with-resources": 0.7021733522415161}